+## Tool-call risk gating
+
+`ADR-0001` (`docs/adr/0001-tool-call-risk-gating.md`) generalizes the
+git-pre-push-hook reasoning below to any agent tool call: `moor run`
+gates a command against a deterministic rule table (`cli/src/decision.rs`)
+host-side, before `docker exec` runs it, precisely because an in-sandbox
+hook on the agent CLI would have the same weakness a baked-in git hook
+does. A `Deny` verdict is recorded in the audit chain and blocks the
+command outright; there is no model or "ask" verdict yet.
+
 ## Why not a git pre-push hook for detecting code leaving the sandbox
 
 An earlier version of this plan considered baking a `pre-push` git hook
