+# Design — tool-call-risk-gate
+
+## Approach
+
+The seam is `run_cmd::run`, the one place a `moor run`/`moor keel` argv
+crosses from host to `docker exec`. Nothing upstream of it (main.rs's
+dispatch, keel_cmd.rs's argv-building) needs to change — both already
+call `run_cmd::run`, so gating there covers both callers for free.
+
+1. New `cli/src/decision.rs`: a pure `pub fn evaluate(cmd: &[String]) ->
+   Verdict` where `Verdict` is `Allow` or `Deny { rule_id, reason }`. Three
+   rules, checked in a fixed order, first match wins:
+   `credential_access` (path segment matches `.ssh`, `.aws`, `.netrc`,
+   `id_rsa`, `.pem`), `boundary_escape` (an arg contains `docker.sock`, or
+   `cmd[0] == "sudo"`), `destructive` (`cmd[0] == "rm"`, a recursive+force
+   flag present, and a target of `/`, `/workspace`, or `~`). No rule
+   matching is `Allow`. No state, no I/O — this is what AC-2/3/4's unit
+   tests exercise directly.
+2. `run_cmd::run` calls `decision::evaluate(cmd)` before building the
+   `docker exec` argv. `Deny` calls a new `audit::log_decision(name, &m,
+   "deny", rule_id, cmd)` (mirrors `log_exec`'s redaction) and returns
+   `Err` before `proc::run_inherit` is ever called — AC-5. `Allow` falls
+   through to the existing, untouched exec/push path — AC-6.
+3. `docs/adr/0001-tool-call-risk-gating.md`: context (the spike, the
+   pre-push-hook precedent this generalizes), decision (host-side gate in
+   `run_cmd::run`; an in-sandbox hook is signal only), consequences (what
+   this does and does not cover, pointing at the spec's Out of scope).
+4. `docs/THREAT-MODEL.md` gets one new bullet under "What counts as a
+   breakout" or a short new section cross-referencing the ADR — not a
+   rewrite of the existing text.
+
+No new dependency, no daemon, no socket. `decision::evaluate` is written
+so a later spec can swap the fixed rule table for a model-backed
+`DecisionModel` trait without touching `run_cmd::run`'s call site.
